---Binds warehouse columns to a custom property definition. Account sources read a materialized
---view column and sync onto matching accounts; person and group sources read either an imported
---warehouse table or a materialized view, and sync onto matching persons or groups on every
---warehouse run of what they read.
---@class posthog.custom_property_definitions.CustomPropertySource
---@field id string
---@field definition string UUID of the custom property definition this source feeds. One source per definition.
---@field saved_query? string|distilled.Null UUID of the data-warehouse saved query to read from. Required for an account source. For a person or group source it must be a materialized view, and is one of the two binding options. Mutually exclusive with external_data_schema.
---@field external_data_schema? string|distilled.Null Person and group sources only: UUID of the warehouse schema (an imported table) to read from. Mutually exclusive with saved_query; a person or group source sets exactly one.
---@field source_column? string|distilled.Null Account sources only: column in the view whose value is written to the property.
---@field column_property_map? any Person and group sources only: {warehouse_column: property_name} mapping the columns this source writes onto the person or group.
---@field column_descriptions? any Person and group sources only: {warehouse_column: description} giving each mapped column a human-facing description, seeded from the warehouse column's information_schema description. Optional per column.
---@field key_column string Column whose value identifies the target: an account's external_id for account sources, the person's distinct_id for person sources, or the group key for group sources.
---@field is_enabled? boolean Whether the source syncs. Auto-disabled after repeated failures or a missing view; re-enabling resets the failure count.
---@field consecutive_failures number Consecutive failed sync runs; the source auto-disables at the cap.
---@field last_synced_at string|distilled.Null When the most recent sync run finished.
---@field last_sync_error string|distilled.Null Error summary from the last run, or null if it succeeded.
---@field created_at string
---@field created_by number|distilled.Null
---@field updated_at string|distilled.Null
---@field sync_frequency_interval_seconds number|distilled.Null Person and group sources only: how often the bound table or view runs, in seconds. Null for account sources, or when the schedule is unavailable — including a view whose frequency is set on its data-modeling DAG.
---@field next_sync_at string|distilled.Null Person and group sources only: approximate time of the next scheduled run (last run + interval). Approximate — drifts if the schedule was paused. Null for account sources, if never run, or when the interval is unavailable.
---@field latest_run posthog.custom_property_definitions.CustomPropertySyncRun|distilled.Null Person and group sources only: the most recent sync/backfill run, or null if none yet.
---@field external_data_source string|distilled.Null Table-bound person and group sources only: UUID of the warehouse source owning the schema, so the UI can link to the table. Null for account sources, view-bound sources, or when unavailable.
---@field table_name string|distilled.Null Person and group sources only: what this source reads, as it is named in HogQL — the imported table, or the view. Null for account sources or when unavailable.
---@field saved_query_name string|distilled.Null View-bound person and group sources only: the materialized view's name, so the UI can tell a view-backed source from a table-backed one. Null for account and table-bound sources.

---One warehouse-backed custom property sync run.
